{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYzwzdA5m6yTx936qrk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In VoiceArena's English full-session benchmark, which covers overlapping speech and 2 to 8 speakers, NVIDIA's Nemotron 3.5 Transcribe drops 8.32% of reference words, while the median across the 14 systems tested is about 31%. Overlapping speech is where many systems lose words, and a meeting transcript with missing sentences is hard to use whoever gets the credit.\n\nThe design explains part of this. Speaker cues from NVIDIA's Sortformer model are passed to the language model together with the acoustic features, so Transcribe can tag each speaker turn while it generates text. A common alternative is to transcribe first and attach speakers to words in a later step. NVIDIA says the model does not rely solely on that later step, though the article does not test the two designs against each other, so the benchmark results cannot be credited to this choice alone.\n\nOn VoiceArena, Transcribe has the lowest concatenated minimum-permutation WER at 32.4%, ahead of NVIDIA Multitalker Parakeet with Nemotron 3 Diarization at 34.2%, and it ranks first in both in-person and online settings. On David AI's diarization track across 21 languages it posts the lowest diarization error rate of the 14 systems, 18.26%, against 18.38% for NVIDIA's dedicated diarization model. NVIDIA models hold the top two places on both leaderboards.\n\nA cpWER of 32.4% is a leading score and still means errors equal to about a third of the reference words once speaker labels are matched, on a hard benchmark with overlap. That fits the model card's advice to spot-check names, speaker changes and answers against the recording. In practice, a transcript that labels speakers still needs a human check before anyone relies on who said what."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1308,"cache_read_input_tokens":8686,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1308},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36151e93-a157-48a1-8c2d-a29815113b4f","uuid":"8d02eb39-bc6c-4d24-b06f-0384f27c417d","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:31:01.958Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYzwYbd4p4aVHKE8unX"}
